<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρᾰβέω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ],
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄραβος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rattle, ring,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (mostly in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>), always of armour, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δούπησεν δὲ πεσὼν ἀράβησε δὲ τεύχε᾽
					ἐπ᾽ αὐτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.42
				</span></i>
			, al.; of the teeth, <i>gnash,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀραβεῖ δ᾽ ἁ γνάθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					21.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> trans.,
				<i>gnash, grind,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδόντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					249
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.281
			</span></i>.</div>
